  "version": "1.9.9",
  "changelog": "Two things. (1) Building jumps carry the building: from the Building Editor, click a road in the 3D view and the Map Editor now opens with the building itself drawn where it belongs \u2014 a pale-blue ghost outline with its name \u2014 its road already selected, and the view framed to show both. The ghost is reference only and clears the moment you click, scroll or turn the view yourself. (2) Universal controls everywhere: drag pans, the wheel zooms, + and - zoom, and Control+drag rotates \u2014 the same in the map, the elevation pane and the 3D inspector (the inspector follows them while it is live).",
